    {
      "id": "evidence-001-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Two kernels, independently. `Kernel::axiom_footprint` walks this declaration's transitive dependencies in the IMPORTED environment and reports `Classical.choice, Quot, Quot.lift, Quot.mk, Quot.sound, propext` -- six names, because our kernel counts the whole quotient package as trusted `Quotient` declarations; a real Lean 4.30.0 binary's `#print axioms Classical.em` reports `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` -- three names. The first three entries are the assumptions the IMPORT adds and the constructed `kernel-lean` route does not make: that the exporter faithfully rendered Lean's environment, that our NDJSON-to-kernel-term translation preserves meaning, and that the delivered bytes are the producer's intended export -- format 3.1 has no footer, so completion is relative to the bytes handed over, which `axeyum-lean-import`'s own documentation states. They are why `axiom_footprint: []` is unavailable on this route and the validator rejects it (ADR-0454).",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
